  "methods": "All-candidate review only; no triplet is selected and no cross-record response is fitted. Use the configured per-file volume schedule, not recording length: IM_15-17 20s/level; IM_53-56 30s/level. First-level start=0 remains an assumption unless overridden. Use configurable central windows (notebook default: 26s for 30s IM blocks). Split into complete nonoverlapping subwindows, 4s by default; report the trailing remainder omitted from stability only. The main amplitude estimator uses the entire central window. Plot the existing target-conditioned peak estimator near 100Hz (target_hz +/- target_halfwidth_hz): linear interpolation at timestamp-derived rate, mean removal, periodic Hann, padded FFT and log-amplitude three-point peak interpolation. Peak amplitude is in counts; it is distinct from raw RMS and peak-to-peak. No smoothing of amplitudes; gaps and unsupported windows remain flagged/exported. Time axis uses actual recording-relative window centers. Different dwell groups do not share volume timing; additional per-dwell panels show correct boundaries. Subwindows describe within-record stability, not independent experimental repeats. Source timestamps, ADC values and files are unchanged. PNG and editable SVG exports.",
